<title>ITALY: Specialists bid for 11 bln lire of Italy Btp.</title>
<headline>Specialists bid for 11 bln lire of Italy Btp.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Specialist bond traders bid for 11 billion lire of 10-year fixed-rate bonds (BTP) against the Italian Treasury's offer of 150 billion lire of paper.</p>
<p>Earlier, the Treasury received bids for 2.33 trillion lire at the open auction for the July 1, 2006 paper, against 1.5 trillion lire worth of certificates on offer.</p>
<p>The auction price was set at 103.20 from 99.60 at the previous Btp sale on September 16.</p>
</text>
